    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0864" n="856" xml:id="pg856"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1048: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-06T15:00:00+00:00">December 6, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 6—11:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1396. From Rublee. Your 732, November 30, 7 p.m. We immediately urged upon the
                    German intermediary, who is arranging the meeting at Brussels on
                        Thursday,<anchor n="80" xml:id="d828-f1"/> the possibility of having a
                    British financial expert accompany Pell. He has now replied that his principals
                    would rather call off the meeting than have a British representative present.
                    They are prepared to make a business proposition to Pell as Assistant Director
                    of the Committee and are prepared to have Cotton<anchor n="81" xml:id="d828-f2"
                    /> present as my personal representative.</p>
                <p>I might add that Cotton is fully qualified to report on financial matters.
                    [Rublee.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
